    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Mineral buildup can cause a knocking sound due to the accumulation of minerals like limescale on the interior of the tank, which can create rust spots that strike a solid spot when the water flows. This type of noise is often rhythmic and can increase in frequency and intensity over time. Unfortunately, severe mineral buildup can be difficult to reverse on your own and is often best left to a professional plumber, especially if the issue has escalated to a noisy, or leaking, tank. However, a plumber can assess the situation and provide guidance on the best course of action.",
